    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.122.1",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-129975-gpgme",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-129975 high vulnerability for gpgme package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gpgme. When processing crafted input, an early return following memory reallocation can leave internal buffer pointers referencing previously freed memory, resulting in a double-free condition during cleanup. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability to corrupt process memory, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution or a Denial of Service (DoS) crash."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-129975",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-129975\nSeverity: high\nPackage: gpgme\nVersion: 1.15.1-6.el9\nFix Version: \nType: rpm\nLocation: /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite\nData Namespace: redhat:distro:redhat:9\nLink: [CVE-2026-129975](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-129975)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-129975**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | gpgme  | 1.15.1-6.el9  |   | rpm  | /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite  | redhat:distro:redhat:9  | [CVE-2026-129975](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-129975)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:rpm/rocky/gpgme@1.15.1-6.el9?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=rocky-9.9\u0026upstream=gpgme-1.15.1-6.el9.src.rpm"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119586-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119586 high vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the SQLite command-line interface. This vulnerability allows an attacker to achieve arbitrary command execution by convincing a user to run the recovery command on a specially crafted database. Because the recovery process fails to sanitize embedded shell instructions within the database schema, piping or re-importing the recovered output into the command-line shell executes operating system commands with the privileges of the running user."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-119586",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119586\nSeverity: high\nPackage: sqlite-libs\nVersion: 3.34.1-11.el9_8\nFix Version: \nType: rpm\nLocation: /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite\nData Namespace: redhat:distro:redhat:9\nLink: [CVE-2026-119586](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-119586)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-119586**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | sqlite-libs  | 3.34.1-11.el9_8  |   | rpm  | /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite  | redhat:distro:redhat:9  | [CVE-2026-119586](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-119586)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:rpm/rocky/sqlite-libs@3.34.1-11.el9_8?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=rocky-9.9\u0026upstream=sqlite-3.34.1-11.el9_8.src.rpm"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
