              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92390 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in curl. When the command-line tool is executed with the remote header name option to prevent overwriting existing files, a malicious server can bypass this protection by returning an intermediate HTTP 103 (Early Hints) response or through specific header ordering. This flaw allows an attacker controlling a remote server to overwrite existing local files on the client system."
