            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107496-openssl",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107496 medium vulnerability for openssl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in openssl. An attacker who can supply a specially crafted recipient certificate to an application performing Cryptographic Message Syntax (CMS) encryption can trigger an infinite loop, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This issue occurs when an elliptic curve (EC) certificate specifies an invalid group order, causing the ephemeral key generation process to retry indefinitely while waiting for a valid key. Consequently, the affected application process hangs and consumes a CPU core until it is terminated."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-107496",
              "help": {
