                "text": "CVE-2026-119379 high vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in SQLite's session extension. A local attacker can supply a specially crafted changeset containing inconsistent table definitions, causing the application to write data past allocated memory boundaries. This heap-based buffer overflow results in memory corruption, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution or a Denial of Service (DoS)."
