              "id": "CVE-2026-119375-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119375 medium vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in SQLite. A local attacker can exploit this vulnerability by providing a crafted database and a Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) file configured with an undersized page size. This mismatch causes SQLite to read uninitialized page-cache memory when executing queries on oversized records, resulting in information disclosure of internal pointers and other database rows."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-119375",
