            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-126765-glibc",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-126765 low vulnerability for glibc package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in glibc. This vulnerability allows an attacker to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) through a double-free condition in file pattern-matching (glob) functions. Under constrained memory conditions, an attacker who controls the input pattern can force a memory allocation failure during directory name processing. When recovering from the error, the application releases the same memory block twice, resulting in a crash or potential memory corruption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-126765",
