              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119591 medium vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in SQLite. This vulnerability allows an attacker to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) by crashing the host application. By supplying a specially crafted database file or SQL query that performs a count operation over a large multi-row VALUES clause, an attacker can trigger excessive recursion during view optimization. This results in stack exhaustion when freeing internal query expressions, terminating the application process."
