              "id": "CVE-2026-124851-libzstd",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-124851 high vulnerability for libzstd package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in zstd. When decompressing streaming data, the decompression engine fails to properly invalidate expired frame history after the output buffer wraps. An attacker could exploit this flaw by providing specially crafted compressed input with malformed offsets to an application that reuses decompression contexts. This issue can lead to information disclosure by exposing uninitialized memory or residual data from earlier decompression operations."
              },
