              "id": "CVE-2026-95690-openssl",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-95690 medium vulnerability for openssl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSL. A remote attacker can cause excessive memory consumption leading to a Denial of Service (DoS) by sending crafted, out-of-sequence Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) handshake fragments. Because OpenSSL allocates a full message-length reassembly buffer for each buffered fragment, an attacker can exhaust system memory resources using a relatively small volume of network traffic."
              },
