            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-115819-glibc",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-115819 medium vulnerability for glibc package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in glibc. An attacker who supplies input to an application using wide scanf functions can trigger an out-of-bounds write, potentially leading to memory corruption or a Denial of Service (DoS) via an application crash. This issue occurs because the wide scanf family of functions writes an extra null byte past the end of the destination buffer when a converted multibyte string exactly fills the allocated space."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-115819",
              "help": {
