              "id": "CVE-2026-84786-openssl",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-84786 medium vulnerability for openssl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSL. When a Transport Layer Security (TLS) client configured with DNS-based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) processes an unusual combination of certificates and TLSA records, a null pointer dereference can occur. A remote attacker or malicious server can exploit this condition to crash the client application, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS)."
              },
