            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-100290-glibc",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-100290 low vulnerability for glibc package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in glibc. When an application compiles or matches regular expressions under system memory pressure, memory allocation failures can cause internal memory tracking errors, leading to accessing or releasing memory blocks that have already been freed. An attacker who provides regular expressions or target strings to an affected application could trigger this flaw, resulting in an application crash and a denial of service (DoS)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-100290",
