            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107493-openssl",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107493 low vulnerability for openssl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSL. When an application provides an existing stack of certificate structures to PEM parsing functions, such as PEM_X509_INFO_read_bio_ex(), and the read operation fails, OpenSSL deallocates all entries in the stack while retaining pointers to the freed memory. A remote attacker can supply malformed Privacy-Enhanced Mail (PEM) data to trigger a read failure. If the calling application subsequently accesses or frees the affected stack, it can cause memory corruption or an application crash resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-107493",
              "help": {
