            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-1485-glib2",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-1485 low vulnerability for glib2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in Glib's content type parsing logic. This buffer underflow vulnerability occurs because the length of a header line is stored in a signed integer, which can lead to integer wraparound for very large inputs. This results in pointer underflow and out-of-bounds memory access. Exploitation requires a local user to install or process a specially crafted treemagic file, which can lead to local denial of service or application instability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-1485",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-1485\nSeverity: low\nPackage: glib2\nVersion: 2.68.4-29.el9_9.1\nFix Version: \nType: rpm\nLocation: /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite\nData Namespace: redhat:distro:redhat:9\nLink: [CVE-2026-1485](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-1485)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-1485**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | glib2  | 2.68.4-29.el9_9.1  |   | rpm  | /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite  | redhat:distro:redhat:9  | [CVE-2026-1485](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-1485)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:rpm/rocky/glib2@2.68.4-29.el9_9.1?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=rocky-9.9\u0026upstream=glib2-2.68.4-29.el9_9.1.src.rpm"
                ],
                "security-severity": "2.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119377-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "RpmMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119377 low vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in SQLite. When processing queries that use a RIGHT or FULL JOIN with a USING clause, SQLite fails to validate authorization restrictions on all joined tables. An attacker capable of submitting SQL queries can exploit this flaw to bypass access control restrictions and read protected column data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-119377",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119377\nSeverity: low\nPackage: sqlite-libs\nVersion: 3.34.1-11.el9_8\nFix Version: \nType: rpm\nLocation: /var/lib/rpm/rpmdb.sqlite\nData Namespace: redhat:distro:redhat:9\nLink: [CVE-2026-119377](https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-119377)",
